     "problem_md": "The diagram shows a test tube containing ammonium chloride that has been heated gently.\n\n![thermal-decomposition-of-ammonium-chloride](assets/001-thermal-decomposition-of-ammonium-chloride.png)\n\nWhich two gases are present at position Y?",
     "solution_md": "**Final answer:** **The correct answer is A**\n\n- When the ammonium chloride is heated it decomposes to form ammonia and hydrogen chloride:\n\nNH<sub>4</sub>Cl (s) → NH<sub>3 </sub>(g) + HCl (g)\n\n- As the gases cool down they recombine to form ammonium chloride\n- A reversible reaction occurs:\n\nNH<sub>4</sub>Cl (s) ⇌ NH<sub>3 </sub>(g) + HCl (g)",
